import Mathlib

/-!
# §3 preamble: the weak limit of the counting measures (Lemma `GHP_convergence`)

Reference: arXiv:2603.13798, §3, Lemma `lem:GHP_convergence`.

The proof of that lemma ends with:

> In particular, the values of any subsequential weak limit on the algebra
> generated by level cells are uniquely determined. […] Thus all boundaries in
> the cell algebra are `μ`-null, and a standard monotone class argument yields a
> unique weak limit measure on `Ξ_M`.

This file proves that final step, in the generality in which it is used:

* `probabilityMeasure_ext_of_piSystem` — two Borel probability measures agreeing
  on a π-system that generates the σ-algebra coincide (this is the "monotone
  class argument"; the level cells and their finite intersections form such a
  π-system on `Ξ_M`);
* `tendsto_of_forall_subseq_limit` — on a compact metric space, if every
  subsequential weak limit of a sequence of probability measures equals `ν`,
  then the sequence converges weakly to `ν` (compactness of the space of
  probability measures replaces tightness);
* `tendsto_of_subseq_limits_agree_on_piSystem` — the combination actually used:
  if every subsequential limit takes the prescribed values `ν(Λ)` on the cells,
  the whole sequence converges weakly to `ν`.

The remaining ingredients of Lemma `GHP_convergence` — the cell-mass asymptotics
`μ_{Ξⁿ}(Λ) → c_i ρ(M)^{-m}` and the nullity of the finite-born points — are in
`RequestProject/Section3/Recursions.lean` and
`RequestProject/Section31/CellMass.lean`.
-/

namespace IGS.Sec31

open MeasureTheory Filter Topology

/--
**The monotone-class step.**  Two Borel probability measures which agree on a
π-system generating the σ-algebra are equal.  On `Ξ_M` the π-system is the
family of level cells (closed under finite intersections up to null boundaries),
whose masses are pinned down by the Perron asymptotics.
-/
theorem probabilityMeasure_ext_of_piSystem {X : Type*} [inst : MeasurableSpace X]
    (C : Set (Set X)) (hC : IsPiSystem C) (hgen : MeasurableSpace.generateFrom C = inst)
    (mu nu : ProbabilityMeasure X) (h : ∀ s ∈ C, (mu : Measure X) s = (nu : Measure X) s) :
    mu = nu := by
  apply ProbabilityMeasure.toMeasure_injective
  refine MeasureTheory.ext_of_generate_finite C hgen.symm hC h ?_
  simp

/--
**From subsequential limits to convergence.**  On a compact metric space the
probability measures form a compact space, so a sequence all of whose
subsequential weak limits equal `ν` converges weakly to `ν`.
-/
theorem tendsto_of_forall_subseq_limit {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] [CompactSpace X]
    [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X]
    (mu : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure X) (nu : ProbabilityMeasure X)
    (h : ∀ idx : ℕ → ℕ, Tendsto idx atTop atTop → ∀ l : ProbabilityMeasure X,
      Tendsto (fun k => mu (idx k)) atTop (𝓝 l) → l = nu) :
    Tendsto mu atTop (𝓝 nu) := by
  refine tendsto_of_subseq_tendsto fun ns hns => ?_
  obtain ⟨l, -, φ, hφ, hconv⟩ :=
    (isCompact_univ (X := ProbabilityMeasure X)).tendsto_subseq (x := fun k => mu (ns k))
      (fun k => Set.mem_univ _)
  refine ⟨φ, ?_⟩
  rw [← h (fun k => ns (φ k)) (hns.comp hφ.tendsto_atTop) l hconv]
  exact hconv

/--
**Lemma `GHP_convergence`, final step.**  If every subsequential weak limit of
the normalised counting measures gives the cells their prescribed masses, then
the whole sequence converges weakly to the measure determined by those masses.
-/
theorem tendsto_of_subseq_limits_agree_on_piSystem {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] [CompactSpace X]
    [inst : MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X]
    (C : Set (Set X)) (hC : IsPiSystem C) (hgen : MeasurableSpace.generateFrom C = inst)
    (mu : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure X) (nu : ProbabilityMeasure X)
    (h : ∀ idx : ℕ → ℕ, Tendsto idx atTop atTop → ∀ l : ProbabilityMeasure X,
      Tendsto (fun k => mu (idx k)) atTop (𝓝 l) →
        ∀ s ∈ C, (l : Measure X) s = (nu : Measure X) s) :
    Tendsto mu atTop (𝓝 nu) :=
  tendsto_of_forall_subseq_limit mu nu fun idx hidx l hl =>
    probabilityMeasure_ext_of_piSystem C hC hgen l nu (h idx hidx l hl)

end IGS.Sec31
